  "notes": "City Morgue's in-house producer and third member, working to the group's own stated brief: \"a modern take on nu-metal. It's more trap, with more 808s and high-hats.\" The load-bearing parameter is the guitar harmony: root-and-5th power chords from drop-tuned samples, which the engine has no chord type for. `susOrDimProb` is 0.48 — the highest in this batch — with `extensions.triad` at 0.95 and `voicing.style` `open`, because a sus voicing is the closest thing the generator has to a chord with no third. Tritone and b2 accents are `halfStepDissonance` 0.44 with `locrian` and `phrygian` weighted over natural minor, and \"queasy synth detuning\" is why `timbreHint` is `supersaw_guitar_hybrid` rather than a plain guitar. The riff is drop-tuned, so `melody.register` sits at 50–74 — more than an octave below the genre's bell register and the lowest lead in this batch. \"808 kick doubled by a metal kick sample ... sampled double-kick bursts under breakdowns\" is `kick.densityPerBar` reaching 7 with `tom` and `crash` in `percs.lanes` for the crash accents on 8-bar boundaries; \"whole bus clipped\" is a compressed high `velocityTiers` block. The 808 in unison with the guitar root, short-to-medium decay, is `followRootsProb` 0.96 with `sustain` `staccato`. ⚠ `medium` matches the research: his role, credits, chart data and the group's stated brief are documented, but the paragraph marks per-parameter detail `[LOW-CONF]` as inference from the records. The INFERRED parameters here are the drum placement numbers, the `velocityTiers` block and the 808 decay setting; the harmony (\"static i or i–VI–VII\") and the riff description are not.",
